  'A DHS final rule of 17 July 2026 establishes a fixed period of admission and an extension-of-stay procedure for F students', 'CONTRADICTS a sibling authority and that is why it is recorded here. USCIS still describes F and J admission as duration of status on pages last reviewed in 2024 and 2025; SEVP announces on 17 July 2026 that a final rule replaces it with a fixed period. Both are DHS. Where two components of one department disagree, the later dated statement is reported as an announcement and the earlier one is left standing as quoted — resolving it ourselves would publish a rule neither page states.',
